// Title: RDP Over Reverse SSH Tunnel
// Sigma ID: 5f699bc5-5446-4a4a-a0b7-5ef2885a3eb4
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Samir Bousseaden
// Date: 2019-02-16 | Modified: 2024-03-12
// ATT&CK: command-and-control, T1572, lateral-movement, T1021.001
// Tags: car.2013-07-002
// Description: Detects svchost hosting RDP termsvcs communicating with the loopback address and on TCP port
//   3389
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://twitter.com/cyb3rops/status/1096842275437625346
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/network_connection/net_connection_win_rdp_reverse_tunnel.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceNetworkEvents
| where (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\svchost.exe" and LocalPort == 3389) and (ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "127.0.0.0/8") or ipv4_is_in_range(RemoteIP, "::1/128"))
